[ti:2-01-电子商务]
[00:00.00]As can be seen from the above bar chart,
[00:03.33]volume of global electronic commerce transactions has increased rapidly during the past 15 years.
[00:12.07]In 2000,
[00:12.80]it was almost 2 billion dollars,
[00:15.61]while the number reached 90 billion in 2010.
[00:19.46]By 2020,
[00:20.19]the number jumped dramatically to 300 billion dollars,
[00:25.08]150 times that of 2000.
[00:27.06]Why is electronic commerce booming nowadays?
[00:31.12]Several causes contribute to this phenomenon.
[00:35.29]Above all,
[00:36.22]the availability of computers is the foremost contributor and the rapid development of information technology enables nearly everybody to have access to the computer and the Internet.
[00:52.57]Nowadays,
[00:53.50]the Internet is no longer a stranger to common people.
[00:58.19]What is more,
[00:59.33]the Internet technology is becoming increasingly mature.
[01:04.54]People who at first do not trust business transactions online now become convinced that electronic commerce is extremely convenient and efficient.
[01:17.65]Last but not least,
[01:19.32]electronic commerce is the fastest way so far to make transactions across far distances.
[01:27.13]The booming electronic commerce undoubtedly contributes to the prosperity of the world economy.
